target: internal/report/post.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestAFailedLabelRemovalIsReported'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    four of applyLabel's five gh calls discarded their result — not even bound to a variable — while the comment above said every call was best-effort, which described only the add. A removal that failed left the PREVIOUS run's label standing beside the new one, the add still succeeded, and the diag still said the label had moved: a PR advertising two convergences at once with nothing anywhere saying so. Discarding the stream that says why a gh call failed is the exact defect this whole slice exists to stop.
